# Railway Brawler: the counters are put on "it", the creature that entered, and X is read as the ability resolves. Bot1 casts Memnite with the
# Brawler out (plotted turn 1, cast free turn 3); with the trigger on the stack Bot2 (a Mox Ruby played on turn 2) Lightning Bolts the Memnite. It
# dies (the trigger's subject is now a new object in the graveyard, CR 400.7), the trigger resolves and does nothing (no error, no
# counters on any other creature: the Brawler is still 5/5), and the Memnite in Bot1's graveyard is a plain card.
# Ornithopter (0/2) then enters: X is its power, zero, so no counters (0/2, not 1/3).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Mox Emerald
Railway Brawler
Memnite
Ornithopter
Plains x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Lightning Bolt
Plains x20

[Actions]
